==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem}} *{{term||akusi|lang=gem}}, from an earlier *{{term||akwusi-|lang=gem}}, possibly from {{proto|Indo-European|ak-}}, *{{term||ok-|lang=pie|sharp, pointed}}.  Cognate with Old Frisian {{term|axa|lang=ofs}}, Old Saxon {{term|akus|lang=osx}} (Saxon {{term|ęx|lang=nds}}), Dutch {{term|aaks|lang=nl}}, Old High German {{term|ackus|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Axt|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|øx|lang=non}}, {{term|ax|lang=non}}, Gothic {{term|𐌰𐌵𐌹𐌶𐌹|lang=got|sc=Goth}}{{rfr|got}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/æks/|lang=ang}}

